{"status":"success","data":[{"siteid":13476,"sitename":"Liten Cap’pesjav’ri","sitedescription":"Glacial origin lake on Magerøya Island. The local bedrock is principally metamorphosed Late Proterozoic to Cambrian age sandstones, with quartzite, amphibolite and conglomerate layers. Site is located in tundra, a major component of which are dwarf-shrub communities dominated by Empetrum nigrum ssp. hermaphroditum, with Vaccinium vitis-idaea, V. uliginosum, V. myrtillus, and Betula nana as frequent and locally co-dominant components.","geography":"{\"type\":\"Polygon\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[[[25.36415,71.07382],[25.37327,71.07382],[25.37327,71.07515],[25.36415,71.07515],[25.36415,71.07382]]]}","altitude":38,"recdatecreated":"2016-08-08T05:01:13.000Z","collectionunits":[{"handle":"CAPPESJA","datasets":[{"datasetid":20279,"datasettype":"pollen"}],"collectionunit":null,"collectionunitid":15098,"collectionunittype":"Core"}]}],"message":"Retrieved all tables"}